Package: dtaIPDMA
Type: Package
Title: Robust Statistical Methods for Individual Participant Data Meta-Analysis of Diagnostic Test Accuracy
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Diribsa T.", "Bedada", email = "dtbedada@uwaterloo.ca",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides robust statistical methods for individual participant
    data meta-analysis of diagnostic test accuracy. The initial release
    implements classical and precision-weighted Henze-Zirkler tests for
    assessing the bivariate normality assumption for empirical Bayes
    study-specific effects. The weighted test combines estimated between-study
    heterogeneity with within-study sampling-variance approximations based on
    diagnostic two-by-two tables, and uses parametric bootstrap calibration
    under a fitted bivariate normal generalized linear mixed model. Future
    methodological extensions are planned but not yet implemented.
